<title>UK: CRS trading surplus declines in year.</title>
<headline>CRS trading surplus declines in year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to January 25, 1997</p>
<p>				 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Gross profit	     383.4		  vs 383.4</p>
<p> Trading suplus	   24.05		  vs 33.49</p>
<p> Net sales		  1.54 billion	 vs 1.56 billion</p>
<p>NOTE - Co-operative Retail Services (CRS) is partly owned by the Co-Operative Wholesale Society (CWS), which last week successfully defended a hostile takeover bid from Andrew Regan's Galileo.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
